- # CMIC Skill Scanner
- **DEFENSIVE SECURITY TOOL** - Use this skill to audit other skills before installation.
- This package includes a native Rust binary scanner. No external downloads required.
- ## Package Contents
- | File | Purpose |
- |------|---------|
- | `assets/bin/skillscan` | Native Rust scanner binary |
- | `assets/build/skillscan.sha256` | Binary checksum for verification |
- | `assets/build/build-info.json` | Build metadata (version, platform, checksum) |
- ## Security Guarantees
- This tool **DOES NOT**:
- - Read your credentials, SSH keys, AWS configs, or any identity files
- - Access MEMORY.md, USER.md, SOUL.md, or agent identity files
- - Send data anywhere without your explicit command
- - Modify system files outside your specified workspace
- - Request elevated/sudo permissions
- This tool **ONLY**:
- - Reads skill files you explicitly ask it to scan
- - Writes reports to directories you explicitly specify
- - Optionally sends reports to URLs you explicitly provide (enterprise integration)
- - Uses SHA-256 checksums to verify integrity
- ## Verify Before Running
- The binary checksum is provided in `assets/build/skillscan.sha256`. Verify independently:
- ```bash
- ```bash
- ```bash
- sha256sum assets/bin/skillscan
- cat assets/build/skillscan.sha256
- # Should match: 864f9a0189268139878c06bce7a127687f9e491a070d7c7345d22932c899bcd8
- ```
- ```
- ```
- ## Source Transparency
- Source code available for independent verification:
- - **Gitee**: https://gitee.com/random_player/cmic-skill-scanner
- - **Build from source**: `cargo build --release` (see repo README for reproducible build instructions)
- - **Checksum file in repo**: `releases/v0.4.0/SHA256SUMS` (independently published)
- Note: Binary reports version `0.2.0` internally. Package version tracks the overall release (v0.4.0 on Gitee).
- ## Usage
- ### Single Skill Scan
- ./assets/bin/skillscan review /path/to/skill --format markdown
- ### Batch Scan
- ### External Engine (Optional)
- ./assets/bin/skillscan review /path/to/skill --engine external --format markdown
- ### Enterprise Integration (User Controlled)
- **Network upload only happens when YOU explicitly provide `--upload-url`. You control the destination.**
-   --upload-url https://your-company.example.com/api/report \
- ## Common Commands
- ./assets/bin/skillscan inspect /path/to/skill    # View skill structure
- ./assets/bin/skillscan scan /path/to/skill       # Raw JSON scan result
- ./assets/bin/skillscan review /path/to/skill     # Risk rating summary
- ./assets/bin/skillscan benchmark                 # Performance benchmark
- ## Detection Capabilities
- Native engine includes 31 detection rules covering:
- - Sensitive file access (credential files, private keys)
- - Network operations (DNS exfiltration, tool downloads)
- - Code injection risks (eval, exec patterns)
- - Unicode steganography detection
- - Process manipulation (shell spawn, process control)
